      "value": "@{5b52ba672b29a515be8ff219|full_name}: I don't see your point of reason here.... games like fortnite are in early access and are free. They also have a dev road map, to inform their player base what features are being added and a general date/time to add the feature. You cant tell me that the devs just sit there and basically have no clue where their game is going or what they plan on adding/making. They more than likely have a plan or an idea of what they want to add to the game. The idea behind the roadmap is to inform they players of upcoming features and developments from the game. It could be as simple as \"we plan to add the chair on avatars by the end of October.\" I only put this as a request because I feel like it would keep the community better informed of what the devs are up to. Dev road maps have a potential to go wrong, if the devs don't come through but as long as they put stuff on the roadmap that they are 100% certain they can get done, there should be no reason not to have a roadmap. As for this site, yes it does a good job of communication but there has been stuff under \"planned\" since march of 2017 that we dont have. Like i said this would be a more indepth version of this with time/dates informing us when we could see these things, not just a \"planned\" or in \"progress\".",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
